1
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:54,750
Open your heart. Find your voice.

2
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:43,500
Song for Marion is a music, comedy, romance film
directed by Paul Andrew Williams.

3
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:32,250
Arthur is a grumpy pensioner who can't understand why his wife Marion would want to
embarrass herself singing silly songs with her unconventional local choir.

4
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:21,000
But choir director Elizabeth sees something special in the
reluctant Arthur and refuses to give up on him.

5
00:29:03,750 --> 00:29:09,750
As she coaxes him out of his shell, Arthur realizes
that it is never too late to change.

6
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:58,500
Arthur, played by Terence Stamp.

7
00:40:41,250 --> 00:40:47,250
Marion, played by Vanessa Redgrave.

8
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Elizabeth, played by Gemma Arterton.

9
00:52:18,750 --> 00:52:24,750
James, played by Christopher Eccleston.

10
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:13,500
Brenda, played by Anne Reid.

11
01:03:56,250 --> 01:04:02,250
Charlie, played by Ram John Holder.

12
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
Song for Marion is a 2012 British-German comedy-drama film written and directed by Paul Andrew Williams
and starring Terence Stamp, Gemma Arterton, Christopher Eccleston and Vanessa Redgrave.

13
01:15:33,750 --> 01:15:39,750
The film was released as Unfinished Song in the USA.

14
01:21:22,500 --> 01:21:28,500
The film was nominated for three awards—Best Actor, Best Screenplay, and Best
Supporting Actress—at the 2012 British Independent Film Awards.

15
01:27:11,250 --> 01:27:17,250
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
